Five working diagrams of how this project fits together, straight from the project's own planning docs. Colors are the same CityLink yellow, purple, and cream the site itself uses, pulled from the bus's own livery.

Three are posted unedited. Two others, covering how a release gets proven safe and who decides what, carry internal-only detail in their original form, so simplified public versions stand in for those instead; the originals stay internal.

**How someone becomes a member**, from application through to active (or not).

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-lifecycle.svg" alt="Member lifecycle: submit application, verify email, keyholder claims and tours, one keyholder decides, then assent leads to active, paused, left, or removed." />

**What happens after you're active.** Contributions and other extras stay optional, and separate from membership itself.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-projection-flow.svg" alt="Member projection flow: active membership branches into an optional contribution offer (no contribution, cash or check, or Stripe when live gates pass) and an optional projection queue for mailing list and mailbox, none of which change membership." />

**How a tool moves** from the shelf to your hands and back.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/inventory-custody-flow.svg" alt="Inventory custody flow: scan a tool, check its availability and condition, finalize a loan, then scan it back in, inspect it, and route it to available or quarantine." />

**How a change gets safely onto the site.** Reviewed, built, checked twice, deployed, then confirmed actually serving before it's called done, with a rollback path if something's wrong.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/release-proof-flow-public.svg" alt="Release proof flow: reviewed by another person, built into a release, checked twice (automated tests, then a human check), deployed to the site, confirmed actually serving and not just deployed, then recorded as done; if something's wrong, rolled back to the last working version instead." />

**Who decides what.** Different kinds of decisions go to different people, on purpose.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/launch-authority-flow-public.svg" alt="Launch authority flow: members' personal facts stay private; applications to join go to keyholders, who decide on admission; money and payments are handled separately from membership decisions; releases of the site get the operator's sign-off." />
